[size=5]Cartur's Build Camera[/size]

Equip a hammer near a workbench, press [b]Shift+B[/b], and the camera detaches from your character. Look around and move as usual, build and pick pieces as usual, and put it away with Shift+B again, R, or by unequipping the tool. Works with the hoe, the cultivator, and any modded build tool.

[size=4]Why this exists[/size]

Azumatt's [i]Build Camera Custom Hammers Edition[/i] is deprecated, and the version still on Thunderstore - 1.3.1 - is broken on Valheim 1.0.

Valheim 1.0 dropped the trailing optional bool from [i]ZInput.GetJoyLeftStickX/Y[/i] and [i]GetJoyRightStickX/Y[/i]. C# bakes the resolved argument count into the call site, so that build still references four signatures that no longer exist and throws every frame a controller is read. This fork is that code ported from upstream 1.3.3, recompiled against 1.0.16, and maintained.

[size=4]What it does[/size]

[list]
[*]Detached build camera for any tool with a piece table - vanilla and modded hammers, hoe, cultivator
[*]Its own configurable station range. It does [b]not[/b] widen workbench coverage or player-base protection, so it will not suppress raids
[*]The camera cannot cross terrain. HearthBelow cave floors, walls and ceilings use the same collision path
[*]Optional cozy and minimum-comfort requirement, on camera entry or on camera pickup
[*]Pick up items off the ground through the camera, with a configurable HUD warning when the cozy rule blocks it. Respects wards, and WardIsLove when installed
[*]An equipped Dvergr circlet's light follows the camera - CircletExtended and RaziCirclet slots too. Position, intensity, range, colour and shadows configurable
[*]A Wisplight's demister ball follows the camera, 2.5x clearing range by default
[*]Separate mouse and controller look inversion; optional world-relative panning
[*]ServerSync: configs sync from the server
[/list]

[size=4]Changed in this fork[/size]

[list]
[*]Recompiled for Valheim 1.0.16 - the controller fix above
[*]Default key is Shift+B, not bare B, which collided with common quick-slot binds
[*]Exits build mode on death, and on a portal hop
[*]Refuses to start while the game's own freefly camera is active
[*]Auto-pickup falls back to the vanilla ward check when WardIsLove cannot be resolved
[*]Version handshake uses a minimum-version floor instead of demanding an exact match
[*]Hotbar keys in build camera read the same input vanilla does
[/list]

[size=4]Incompatible with[/size]

ValheimPlus first person mode, and Masa's FirstPerson - both take over the camera. Do not run Azumatt's Build Camera at the same time; this one stands down if it sees it.

